// A first song: the opening of 送别 (Songbie; words 1915, to the tune of "Dreaming of Home and
// Mother", 1868; in the public domain) — the short one, for a computer where a voice sings
// slowly; "the whole song" in the steps opens all of it. The part names its words, `lyrics`
// holds them, the score's row prints them, and the `singer` line is what makes them heard. A
// slur carries one word over two notes. Open the preview and press Play.
title "送别"
poet "李叔同"
composer "John P. Ordway"
octave relative
time 4/4
key c major
tempo 96
part melody { instrument alto  lyrics words }
section A {
  melody {
    g'4 e8( g) c2 | a4 c g2 | g4 c,8( d) e4 d8( c) | d2. r4 |
  }
  lyrics words language chinese {
    长 亭 外 | 古 道 边 | 芳 草 碧 连 | 天 |
  }
}
form { A }
singer female on melody
score { staff melody  lyrics words }
